<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>2026-2027 English Annual Plan – Grade 7</title><style>@page{size:A4 landscape;margin:.45in}body{font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#111;font-size:9pt}h1{text-align:center;font-size:16pt;margin:4px}h2{font-size:11pt}.meta,.themes,.plan,.sign{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}.meta td,.themes th,.themes td,.plan th,.plan td,.sign td{border:1px solid #555;padding:4px;vertical-align:top}.themes th,.plan th{background:#dceaf4;text-align:center}.themes td{font-size:7.5pt}.plan{table-layout:fixed}.plan th{font-size:6.5pt}.plan td{font-size:6.3pt;line-height:1.12}.plan th:nth-child(1){width:7%}.plan th:nth-child(2){width:4%}.plan th:nth-child(3){width:14%}.plan th:nth-child(4){width:19%}.plan th:nth-child(5){width:18%}.plan th:nth-child(6){width:13%}.plan th:nth-child(7){width:12%}.plan th:nth-child(8){width:13%}.note{font-size:8pt}.sign td{height:55px;text-align:center}</style></head><body><div style="text-align:center;font-weight:bold">T.C.<br>MINISTRY OF NATIONAL EDUCATION</div><h1>2026–2027 ENGLISH LANGUAGE COURSE ANNUAL PLAN — GRADE 7</h1><table class="meta"><tr><td><b>School</b><br>____________________</td><td><b>Teacher</b><br>____________________</td><td><b>Grade</b><br>7</td><td><b>Weekly Hours</b><br>4</td><td><b>Programme</b><br>TYMM 2026–2027</td><td><b>Academic Year</b><br>2026–2027</td></tr></table><p class="note"><b>Basis:</b> MEB 2026–2027 working calendar and the applicable English Language Curriculum. Original DijiMedu working document. Review against the current textbook, school/subject-group decisions, BEP provisions and local school planning before approval.</p><h2>THEME / UNIT DISTRIBUTION</h2><table class="themes"><tr><th>No.</th><th>Theme / Unit</th><th>Content Framework</th><th>Indicative Learning Focus</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td><b>Theme 1 – School Life &amp; Education</b></td><td>Extra-curricular activities, competitions, celebrations, school trips and national days</td><td>ENG.7.1 learning-output family</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td><b>Theme 2 – Classroom Life &amp; Learning</b></td><td>Learning strategies, classroom interaction, cooperation and learning experiences</td><td>ENG.7.2 learning-output family</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><b>Theme 3 – Personal Life &amp; Well-being</b></td><td>Well-being, health, habits, preferences and personal expression</td><td>ENG.7.3 learning-output family</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><b>Theme 4 – Family Life &amp; Home</b></td><td>Family life, home responsibilities, relationships and communication</td><td>ENG.7.4 learning-output family</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><b>Theme 5 – Neighbourhood, City &amp; Social Life</b></td><td>City life, social interaction, services, community and civic awareness</td><td>ENG.7.5 learning-output family</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td><b>Theme 6 – Life in the World &amp; Culture</b></td><td>Cultures, traditions, diversity, global communication and respectful interaction</td><td>ENG.7.6 learning-output family</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td><b>Theme 7 – Life in Nature</b></td><td>Nature, environmental responsibility, sustainability and living things</td><td>ENG.7.7 learning-output family</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td><b>Theme 8 – Life in the Universe &amp; Future</b></td><td>Universe, science, technology, future possibilities and responsible innovation</td><td>ENG.7.8 learning-output family</td></tr></table><h2>WEEKLY ANNUAL PLAN</h2><table class="plan"><thead><tr><th>WEEK / DATES</th><th>HOURS</th><th>THEME / UNIT &amp; CONTENT</th><th>LEARNING OUTCOMES &amp; PROCESS COMPONENTS</th><th>LEARNING–TEACHING EXPERIENCES</th><th>DIFFERENTIATION</th><th>ASSESSMENT &amp; EVALUATION</th><th>IMPORTANT DAYS / SCHOOL-BASED PLANNING</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Week 1<br>14 Sept 2026 –<br>18 Sept 2026</td><td>4</td><td><b>Theme 1 – School Life &amp; Education</b><br>Extra-curricular activities, competitions, celebrations, school trips and national days</td><td>ENG.7.1.L/R/V/G/P; ENG.7.1.W1–W6; ENG.7.1.S1–S6 — preparation, comprehension, construction, reconstruction and reflection through integrated language use.</td><td>Activate prior knowledge; introduce contextual input; model target language and vocabulary. Pair/group work, role-play, picture or text-based tasks, short performance/product and age-appropriate digital or visual materials.</td><td>Support: visuals, word banks, sentence frames, modelling, repetition and peer support.<br>Enrichment: extended speaking/writing, choice tasks or mini-project.</td><td>Observation checklist, questioning, exit task, short performance/product, self-assessment and teacher feedback.</td><td>School opening / orientation</td></tr><tr><td>Week 2<br>21 Sept 2026 –<br>25 Sept 2026</td><td>4</td><td><b>Theme 1 – School Life &amp; Education</b><br>Extra-curricular activities, competitions, celebrations, school trips and national days</td><td>ENG.7.1.L/R/V/G/P; ENG.7.1.W1–W6; ENG.7.1.S1–S6 — preparation, comprehension, construction, reconstruction and reflection through integrated language use.</td><td>Activate prior knowledge; introduce contextual input; model target language and vocabulary. Pair/group work, role-play, picture or text-based tasks, short performance/product and age-appropriate digital or visual materials.</td><td>Support: visuals, word banks, sentence frames, modelling, repetition and peer support.<br>Enrichment: extended speaking/writing, choice tasks or mini-project.</td><td>Observation checklist, questioning, exit task, short performance/product, self-assessment and teacher feedback.</td><td>School-based planning as required</td></tr><tr><td>Week 3<br>28 Sept 2026 –<br>02 Oct 2026</td><td>4</td><td><b>Theme 1 – School Life &amp; Education</b><br>Extra-curricular activities, competitions, celebrations, school trips and national days</td><td>ENG.7.1.L/R/V/G/P; ENG.7.1.W1–W6; ENG.7.1.S1–S6 — preparation, comprehension, construction, reconstruction and reflection through integrated language use.</td><td>Practise comprehens